          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/data+analysis"} data analysis
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observable"} observable
            is typically a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi f
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \overset{f}{\longrightarrow} \mathbb{R}^n
            from a given data set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to the set of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-tuple"} n-tuple
            of such (varying in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
            %em iso-hypersurface
            or
            %em level-hypersuface
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/level+set"} level set
            of this observable, hence the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            consisting all those points
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
            on which this observable
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            takes the same given value
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x) = c
          %p
            For example, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a model for the Earth’s atmosphere, and if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            assigns to each point
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
            the atmospheric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pressure"} pressure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p(x)
            at this point – in some suitable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physical+units"} physical units
            and to some suitable approximation –, then an iso-surface for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            is an
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isobar"} isobar
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surface"} surface
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+function"} constant
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pressure"} pressure
          %p
            For such a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/level+set"} level set
            to actually be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypersurface"} hypersurface
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+manifold"} differentiable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submanifold"} submanifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            need to be satisfied, such as that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+function"} differentiable function
            to suitable degree, and, crucially, that its value
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            (whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pre-image"} pre-image
            is formed) is a
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+value"} regular value
          %p
            Phrased this way, the construction of iso-hypersurfaces turns out to be a central topic also in areas of pure mathematics, such as in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+topology"} differential topology
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+theory"} cobordism theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pre-images"} pre-images
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+values"} regular values
            inside
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
            is known as part of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontryagin+construction"} Pontryagin construction
          %p
            Curiously, this means that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontryagin%27s+theorem"} Pontryagin's theorem
            applies to iso-hypersurfaces, saying here that, as the value
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observable"} observable
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            varies, the shape (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"}> topology
            ) of the corresponding iso-hypersurfaces changes (at most) by a
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism"} cobordism
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normally+framed+submanifold"} normally framed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+class"} cobordism class
            of all these hypersurfaces corresponds to the class of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            in the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cohomotopy+theory"} Cohomotopy theory
            of the data set
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            While Pontryagin’s theorem is ancient, the idea that it thus implies the possibility of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+data+analysis"} topological data analysis
            via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cohomotopy+theory"} Cohomotopy theory
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observables"} observables
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+theory"} cobordism theory
            of their iso-hypersurfaces appears only recently (
            %a{:href => "#FranekKrcal16"}> Franek-Krčál 16
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#FranekKrcal17"} Franek-Krčál 17
